    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_55d93b93b5749746667c102f39d299011a73258722de2096c5a0b2350fd25bad",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Li's all-n criterion supplies the target sequence; the selected no-gap resolvent converts its coefficients into Fourier couplings, and the stepwise imaginary boundary value converts those Fourier coefficients by integration by parts into a sum of 1-cos(n*theta_i). This makes nonnegativity manifest inside the constructed unit-circle representation but functions as a conditional reformulation and consistency check, not independent evidence for RH.",
