    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7ddcea0270a28bbe1765f0d5cb961feba8c7867393f2bccd1333b63fc0a48f41",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Nonuniqueness survives successive restrictions. The character action first leaves an arbitrary even component in the Young boundary; constant-density droplet topology narrows this freedom by fixing boundary separation from rho; for the spiky no-gap density, the remaining non-injective boundary still yields multiple monotone, normalized Young branches. The appendix's theta=pi*u(h) argument supplies only a compatibility witness for selecting branch data, not a uniqueness derivation.",
