    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_95340b9314d8dcdbebb993141b96a5fa836169b1b2a9928918aa744e8397eb96",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The character expansion turns trace data into a Young-diagram sum, and Frobenius auxiliary variables acquire spectral meaning when their large-N saddle reproduces both the eigenvalue saddle and the eigenvalue partition function. The complex saddle splits into a spectral equation and a Young-boundary relation; even-function freedom makes the latter nonunique, droplet topology fixes boundary separation, and the complex Omega object packages eigenvalue density, potential derivative, and Young density as distinct marginals.",
