    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_97b46fb81eb66a99d61243d51626b95ed248d48230e1ef4c1ae51ee28234b739",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The main-text spike density is internally cross-checked in two ways: the appendix derives its log-sine structure by taking logarithms of the xi zero product and pairing conjugate unit-circle boundary values, while a second appendix verifies total mass both by direct angular integration with symmetric zero cancellation and by extracting the normalized resolvent coefficient through a contour integral.",
