    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b0b6b5a21b5db48dbefeeb1f3d095cea6ae7ee47707e80518a27d8e9a40fe189",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The log-xi resolvent first yields a zero-marked no-gap density and a Young-droplet boundary whose non-injective graph must be inverted on monotone branches. Independently, the Mellin relation for prime counting rewrites that same resolvent as an integral against the fluctuating part of J, whose inverse also requires branchwise domains. The shared output and parallel local-inverse obstruction motivate the proposed Young/prime correspondence.",
