    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ec8400b4e310c252bf2e546666527ee0095e4217b55554bed36e4875aaf847a4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Completion makes xi entire and exposes its reflection symmetry; the conformal map turns that involution into reciprocal unit-disk geometry, and the selected log-xi resolvent converts mapped zeros into boundary singularities. Its real and imaginary boundary components then expose the same zeros as logarithmic density spikes and force jumps, while Taylor/Cauchy matching carries Li coefficients into the plaquette couplings and action.",
